{"id": "EUVD-2026-97712", "enisaUuid": "7f87b93c-289a-3244-a614-d31fdfeb6b85", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains a use after free vulnerability in the PDF writer when writing CMYK images with JPEG2000 compression. Attackers can supply a crafted CMYK image that, when written to PDF with JPEG2000 compression, causes freed memory to be reused, potentially crashing the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:33:55", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-j39j-wmxg-j8mv", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/3285d692ebf200e9cbeff59d1ccc00caab99ad54", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/966e227a1a8b520ea1652e2eb3ca78b08d3206f5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-use-after-free-in-pdf-writer-via-jpeg2000"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109268", "GHSA-5w2q-9xw9-jg4r"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4c4af81e-4c8e-3c38-b14e-7b9bc7ed5f61", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}, {"id": "8a166c4e-a146-3c43-b3e9-7d558ea816df", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2f68b24d-1a0e-3244-be1a-db81430a7bd8", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}